A||||8||RossT||advantages/disadvantages of recall weatherseal?||||1||
Z||000000||RossT||11-30-2001||12:25 AM||||How many out there are using the recall weatherseal that seals the area between the trunk lid and the rear window?  I am thinking of installing one to keep the rain/snow etc.. off the front exhaust manifold.  But if you seal of that area, don't you forfit some cooling capacity.  GM removed it during the recalls for a reason.<P>What do you think?  <P>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||Haze_Performance||11-30-2001||12:40 AM||||To tell you the truth... I dont think keeping it on can hurt anything. (85/88) I can see the problems with the 84.. I'm putting one back on my '85 this winter..  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/goodlife.gif">    <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="purple">Goto Website - <A HREF="http://www.ClassicFiero.com" TARGET=_blank>Click Here</A> </FONT></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000002||fieroparts.com||11-30-2001||12:51 AM||||Do you think that tiny weather strip is going to keep any amount of heat in....?<P><BR>Ha, fat chance, that's BS put the strip on<BR>and save your exhaust manifold.<P>my 6 1/2 cents <P>||||reg||14
Z||000003||tgowens||11-30-2001||03:39 AM||||I have it on all of my Fieros - it helps keep the engine compartment clean, deflects water away from the manifold when raising the deck lid, and doesn't diminish the cooling at all.<P>More reasons to have it there than not to.......<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature_TGO.jpg"> <P><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
Z||000004||theogre||11-30-2001||08:09 PM||||I still have the weather seal on mine.<P>In mine (87SC), it keeps allot of crap from falling in there, important when parking under a tree, but it seems to direct more water toward my manifold when opening the deck. I simply try to avoid opening a wet deck when the motor is hot. (cracked 2 manifolds before I figured that out.)<P>I doubt it does much one way or the other for cooling. Got real results there by installing the older style vent grates. That louver sheet under the newer style sucks.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">   <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 11-30-2001).]||||reg||1
